{
 "id": "page-cell-bench-science",
 "target": "page",
 "page": "cell-bench.html",
 "goal": "On the cell bench, count 120 live / 12 dead in 4 large squares at dilution 2 (6.00x10^5 live cells/mL, 90.9% viable), enter the chamber factor, sample and target volumes and confluency explicitly, seed and compute doubling time, build a four-point standard curve and read an unknown, a Beer-Lambert concentration and A260/A280/A230 purity, log two 1:4 passages (cumulative PD 4.0), and score a mitotic index -- every calculator driven and every figure held against an oracle.",
